You could create a basic website and reach out to small businesses offering to build their site for a few hundred dollars. All you'll need is a little JavaScript and some free template hosting.

For example, you could make a contact form like this:

<form action="api/business_contact.php" method="POST">
  Name: <input name="name"><br>
  Email: <input name="email"><br>
  <input type="submit" value="Submit">
</form>

And the backend just looks like this:

<?php
$name = $_POST['name'];
$email = $_POST['email'];

$message = "New contact from $name ($email)";

mail('owner@business.com', 'New Contact', $message);

echo "Thanks for contacting us!";
?>

No need for any fancy validation or error handling. If someone tries to submit <b>alert(1)</b> as their name, that's their own fault!

